3. The Government of India has consolidated the multiple existing labour legislations into a unified framework comprising of Labour Godes collectively referred to as New 'Labour Codes' which become effective from 21 Novemeber 2025. The company has reassessed the employee benefits obligations in accordance with the revised definition of wages. Accordingly, based on management assessment and actuarial valuation, an incrimentalliability on account of past service cost in accordance with IND AS19 'Employee Benefits' &lt;BR&gt; 
amounting to Rs. 711.271akhs has been shown under exceptional items in the Statement of Profit and Loss for the quarter and nine months ended December 31 , 2025 . Further in view of the relevant Rules yet to be notified, the company would continue to monitor developments relating to the implimentation of the New Labour Codes and will review its estimates and assumptions on an ongoing basis. &lt;BR&gt; 
